implementation_summary:
  - Added one guarded, deterministic media contribution role helper using `cawPostLifecycleParticipantRoles()` with the canonical fallback.
  - Upload, update, library, and get declarations now use `contributor,author,editor,admin,administrator,superadmin`.
  - `akira.media.delete@1` remains exactly `admin`; this is an explicit decision the owner may reverse.
  - `akira.media.resolve@1` remains untouched.
  - Permissions listing now includes every `akira.*` provider.
  - Permissions role replacement now accepts the empty-string form representation of a nullable `caller_module`.
  - Media navigation manifest roles now match drafting participants.
  - Tests allocate tenant fixtures dynamically and verify fresh declarations, nullable callers, author contribution, admin-only deletion, narrowing, and widening refusal.
  - Documented the future-CMS media authority convention.
  - Fixed mutation seeding to join the active policy version. Measurement showed fixed-version seeding was inert for tenants with active version greater than 1, preventing A1.

